# What the repository keeps of the catalog run (every board's outputs together are about 3 GB).
#
# Kept: everything at the environment and station level (pages, videos, station boards, ranking, profiles) and
# the board folders on the "!" lines below, each with its explainer video. tools/regen_examples.py reads these
# lines: it copies, films and links only these boards, so the pages never point at a board that is not here.
# A full build copied in by hand stays out of git too. To keep another board, add a line for its folder.
/stations/*/*/

# rank 1 of 128: ten boards on one fixture, the biggest batch in the catalog
!/stations/*/usb_dongle_09/
# eight boards programmed over SWD at the same time
!/stations/*/sensor_20/
# KiCad demo: a 6-layer Raspberry Pi CM5 carrier, three per fixture
!/stations/*/CM5_MINIMA_3/
# KiCad demo: the most complex board, 1,123 parts on 10 layers, programmed over JTAG
!/stations/*/jetson-agx-thor-baseboard/
# KiCad demo: the one board that needs station-2 and its large plate
!/stations/*/video/

# Never published: local paths and the state of a run
sources.json
environment-job*
.pcbtestkit-station.json
*.kicad_prl
**/runner/results/
station_video/
station_video_parts/
__pycache__/
